meta {
  name: Accept Shift
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{coreBaseUrl}}:8108/
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{idToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "shiftId": "BB6oxMJdrdFAHcyMXODh"
  }
}

docs {
  functions-core: AcceptShift (port 8108) — the atomic booking transaction
  from ARCHITECTURE.md v2 §4. Sign in as staff-jane or staff-sam first.
  
  Run this request TWICE in a row: the first call returns 200 {"status":
  "booked"}; the second returns 409 SHIFT_ALREADY_BOOKED — the exact
  error-code contract from §4, proven against the real emulator (this isn't
  simulated: two concurrent accepts on the same shift really do race inside
  one Firestore transaction).
  
  Other error cases to try:
    - shiftId that doesn't exist -> 404 SHIFT_NOT_FOUND
    - a nursery account calling this -> 403 NOT_STAFF
    - no Authorization header -> 401 NOT_AUTHENTICATED
}
